WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.205
- This right here

00:00:01.205 --> 00:00:02.038
(screen tapping)

00:00:02.038 --> 00:00:02.940
is the hottest battleground

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:05.520
for the future of automotive revenues.

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:06.353
The dashboard.

00:00:06.353 --> 00:00:08.130
See, while you may only
really use this screen

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:11.040
for music, navigation and calls in the...

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.860
Oh, in the future, it's set
to be used for a lot more.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:15.120
Traditional automakers plan

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:18.630
on using this space to sell a
suite of features and services

00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:20.610
in a market that some analysts estimate

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:24.990
will be worth some $1.5 trillion by 2030.

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:27.090
But at the same time,
tech giants like Apple

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:29.400
and Google are pushing
to gain deeper control

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:32.550
of your vehicle and take
over more of your dash.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:34.860
Now, battle lines are being drawn.

00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:37.500
So who is winning the
battle of the dashboard?

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:38.580
Let's find out.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.930
No, please don't.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:40.920
Quite enough of that.

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:42.330
Now, I know I've said this before,

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:43.590
but if the car that you're driving

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:46.410
doesn't already receive
downloadable upgrades

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:48.030
and updates over the air,

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:49.200
then there's a strong chance

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.570
that the car that you
buy in the future will,

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:52.403
and that's because there's set

00:00:52.403 --> 00:00:54.090
to be quite a lot of money in it.

00:00:54.090 --> 00:00:57.060
Or as Tesla CEO Elon Musk
said in an earnings call.

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:00.210
- [Elon] We could sell
for zero profit for now

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:04.050
and then yield actually
tremendous economics in the future

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:04.920
through autonomy.

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:06.180
- GM has said it expects

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:09.330
to generate between 20 to $25 billion

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:12.733
in revenue from software-enabled
services by 2030.

00:01:12.733 --> 00:01:16.200
Stellantis has forecast
roughly 22.5 billion

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:17.160
for the same time

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.560
and Accenture predicts
that digital services

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:21.930
will make up a whopping 40%

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:24.720
of global automotive revenues by 2040.

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:27.210
Now, that's crucial for these automakers

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:30.030
because right now, they're
struggling to make money on EVs.

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:31.890
- The profit margin on
these are much smaller

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:33.240
because the batteries are still expensive

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:34.440
and they haven't scaled yet.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.140
- That's Mike Colias who
covers autos for WSJ.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:38.460
- For the next decade,

00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:39.690
investors are kind of wondering, well,

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:41.430
how are you gonna bridge that shortfall

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:43.410
in the profit margins that you're used to

00:01:43.410 --> 00:01:44.940
on your big internal combustion?

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:47.580
The answer to an auto executive is, well,

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.440
we're gonna have all this digital revenue

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:51.420
and subscription services.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:53.760
- So what do these
automakers plan on selling?

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:56.100
Well, at the basic level,
there'll be the usual offerings

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:59.160
of music and entertainment,
as well as navigation services

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.860
to things like parking
spots, valets, EV chargers

00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:03.030
and gas stations.

00:02:03.030 --> 00:02:05.730
Then there's subscriptions
to physical in-car options

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:09.090
that used to be add-ons, like
heated seats, more horsepower

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:10.260
or improved handling.

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:12.630
But one of the most lucrative
subscriptions is set

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:14.250
to be autonomous driving.

00:02:14.250 --> 00:02:15.210
It may not be here yet

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:17.970
but that hasn't stopped some
automakers betting big on it.

00:02:17.970 --> 00:02:19.050
Or as Musk said.

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:21.630
- [Elon] We expect our
vehicles over time will be able

00:02:21.630 --> 00:02:24.960
to generate significant
profit through autonomy.

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:26.850
- Now, some of these upgrades
are set to be accessed

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:29.190
through smartphones and computers,

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:31.890
but if automakers are gonna
start selling through the dash,

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:34.410
they're gonna need to get
someone out the way first.

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:35.775
- CarPlay is the smarter,

00:02:35.775 --> 00:02:38.820
safer way to use your iPhone in the car.

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:40.500
- [Narrator] Chances are
your car is compatible

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:41.730
with Android Auto.

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:44.190
- Yep. Apple CarPlay and Android Auto.

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:47.160
See, for years, automakers'
own infotainment systems lagged

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:50.250
behind that of smartphones,
mainly because cars operate

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:52.620
on longer product cycles than smartphones.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:53.453
- 10 plus years ago,

00:02:53.453 --> 00:02:54.570
the car companies I think thought

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:56.640
they could do this interface on their own.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:57.570
They tried.

00:02:57.570 --> 00:03:00.660
The infotainment touchscreens
in the cars weren't very good.

00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:02.520
And so Apple and Google came up

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:05.430
with these solutions to
essentially mirror your phone

00:03:05.430 --> 00:03:06.263
on the touchscreen of the car.

00:03:06.263 --> 00:03:08.880
And a lot of consumers now rely

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:11.550
on this as their main
interface for the car.

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:13.710
- Now, for a while, this
partnership is working.

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:16.050
Dash screens were pretty
small and the smartphones

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:18.930
didn't really have much
interaction with the car itself

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:21.120
but now those screens are getting bigger.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:23.610
- We designed the new Android Auto UI

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:25.830
to take advantage of those larger screens.

00:03:25.830 --> 00:03:26.670
- [George] And tech companies

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:28.410
are reaching deeper into the car.

00:03:28.410 --> 00:03:29.820
- There's an opportunity

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:33.480
for iPhone to play an
even more important role.

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:35.160
- In 2022, Apple announced

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:36.600
that not only would CarPlay be able

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:38.250
to take over the whole dash,

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:40.080
including the instrument cluster

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:42.660
but that the software would
reach far deeper under the hood.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:44.323
- [Narrator] Tune your car's radio

00:03:44.323 --> 00:03:46.560
or change your temperature

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:50.370
without ever leaving
the CarPlay experience.

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:52.020
This is just a taste

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:54.990
of what the next generation
of CarPlay will bring.

00:03:54.990 --> 00:03:57.780
- That means that Apple
could potentially access some

00:03:57.780 --> 00:03:59.250
of the very features

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:01.230
that automakers are trying to monetize.

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:03.060
And we all know how good Apple

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:05.700
and Google are at selling
downloads and subscriptions.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:07.140
- I mean, that's what
Google and Apple do, right?

00:04:07.140 --> 00:04:11.400
I mean they offer you apps and
features to pass your time.

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:14.640
So it's a battle for that space.

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:15.840
- I spoke to Apple and Google

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:18.510
but neither would tell me
about future automotive plans.

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:21.390
But even if Apple and Google
don't monetize their offerings,

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:24.074
their software still takes over the dash.

00:04:24.074 --> 00:04:24.907
(door clicking)

00:04:24.907 --> 00:04:26.730
- If you've got a tech
giant sitting in between you

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:29.490
and your customer, it's
gonna make it a lot harder

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:31.833
to you monetize that stuff.

00:04:32.700 --> 00:04:34.350
- So it may not be much of a surprise

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:37.110
that GM has stopped
supporting Android Auto

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:39.750
and Apple CarPlay on future EV models.

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:43.290
- I know that GM considered
letting CarPlay live alongside

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:45.870
of its new interface,
but they ultimately felt

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:48.210
like they were just gonna
be fighting for eyeballs.

00:04:48.210 --> 00:04:51.510
- That decision was met
with immediate criticism.

00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:53.310
- Yeah, I mean, I heard from
a lot of people who said

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:55.830
I'll never buy another GM car again.

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:59.160
And I think GM knows that and
to that extent, it's a gamble.

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:00.630
- So is this the beginning

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:03.990
of the end for CarPlay
and Android Auto in cars?

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:05.340
Well, not exactly.

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:07.560
See, even though these
softwares won't be supported

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:09.960
in future GM EVs, the company still plans

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:12.090
on running its own infotainment system

00:05:12.090 --> 00:05:14.670
on a version of Android's
operating system.

00:05:14.670 --> 00:05:16.560
So Google will still be in the car

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:18.120
and despite GM's actions,

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:20.790
a few automakers appear
to be following suit.

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:21.780
For now at least.

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:24.870
- I asked a number of
executives from other companies,

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:27.000
almost all of them said, no way.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:29.250
We have no plans to remove
those from the cars.

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:32.550
I think they see that as
potentially hurting sales.

00:05:32.550 --> 00:05:34.320
- But that could all change.

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:36.750
See, right now digital
services only make up

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:39.840
around 5% of automotive revenues.

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:42.450
But as that percentage starts to increase,

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:43.470
don't be surprised

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:47.244
if you see more automakers
start to unplug the smartphone.

00:05:47.244 --> 00:05:49.827
(upbeat music)

